{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>\"Her You have designated for Your servant, for Isaac.\"</b> This is the language of Rashi (Rashi on Genesis 24:14): she is fitting for him, for she performs deeds of kindness and is fit to enter the household of Abraham. \"And thereby I shall know\" — the language of supplication: let me know through her that You have shown kindness to my master. But if so, he should say, \"I shall know that in truth her You have designated for Your servant, for Isaac,\" and it does not connect well. Rather, its meaning is: \"Grant that it happen before me this day\" — the occurrence that the maiden to whom I say, her — that You have designated for Your servant, for Isaac — and thereby perform kindness with my master Abraham, for through her I shall know that You have done kindness with him, if she be of his family, of good intelligence and beautiful appearance. And likewise he says (Genesis 24:43), \"And the maiden is the woman whom YHWH has designated.\""], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:33:54.302609841Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}